., 500m) using low-latency fiber optic cables to synchronize brain activity between individuals.","position":{"start":{"line":63,"column":1},"end":{"line":63,"column":1}},"key":"kai3PuSWAP"}],"key":"V7ud5yx4VJ"}],"key":"rrguJMQ7Sn"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":64,"column":1},"end":{"line":65,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Quantum Bridging: Emerging “Neuro-Quantum Interfaces” aim to translate these bio-harvested electrical signals into qubits, using the MEG fiber’s steady DC output to power local quantum sensors or repeaters.","position":{"start":{"line":64,"column":1},"end":{"line":64,"column":1}},"key":"b0IJqFOKtp"}],"key":"sj9ms2P368"}],"key":"q5WeYZLHX2"}],"key":"ubfp9fRQ7b"}],"key":"HFDg93nyc9"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":69,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Practical Hardware Integration","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"key":"SKHlbqD2Gw"}],"key":"WEq2fScCt6"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":67,"column":1},"end":{"line":69,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":67,"column":1},"end":{"line":67,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Wearable Sensors: The method is being deployed in self-powered finger-motion sensors that encode information via “dot-and-dash” signals (similar to Morse code) based on moisture-material interactions during movement.","position":{"start":{"line":67,"column":1},"end":{"line":67,"column":1}},"key":"khplLrQ20e"}],"key":"swU1GVz8D3"}],"key":"c4WLC0ip9r"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":68,"column":1},"end":{"line":69,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Long-Term Stability: Implementation focuses on non-transient materials like silk fibroin or carbon-based microfibers to ensure the interface remains functional in liquid biological environments.","position":{"start":{"line":68,"column":1},"end":{"line":68,"column":1}},"key":"jksvOXKTx7"}],"key":"kOt4TvHE2l"}],"key":"H41BXxRkuS"}],"key":"xyVao1tE08"}],"key":"i1RA1HSJty"}],"key":"t753WDLEi0"},{"type":"heading","depth":1,"position":{"start":{"line":70,"column":1},"end":{"line":70,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"DoDIN Strategic Integration","position":{"start":{"line":70,"column":1},"end":{"line":70,"column":1}},"key":"lP7yEnz3hU"}],"identifier":"dodin-strategic-integration","label":"DoDIN Strategic Integration","html_id":"dodin-strategic-integration","implicit":true,"key":"e8yYf65OFz"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":71,"column":1},"end":{"line":71,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Department of Defense (DoD) is implementing these advanced neural and energy methods through several key initiatives:","position":{"start":{"line":71,"column":1},"end":{"line":71,"column":1}},"key":"rmPuhahmUu"}],"key":"oVU40IU8BF"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":72,"column":1},"end":{"line":80,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":72,"column":1},"end":{"line":73,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":72,"column":1},"end":{"line":72,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Self-Powered Network Nodes","position":{"start":{"line":72,"column":1},"end":{"line":72,"column":1}},"key":"n8bYq068ah"}],"key":"rXEuOPS24a"},{"type":"text","value":":\nMEG fibers provide autonomous power for implantable neural devices without requiring external batteries, which are a vulnerability in field environments. The DoDIN utilizes these self-sustaining fibers to power sensors embedded directly into fiber-optic backbones for physical security and health monitoring.","position":{"start":{"line":72,"column":1},"end":{"line":72,"column":1}},"key":"DcMaBkuDre"}],"key":"fskHinvoJZ"}],"key":"SIdgzuJfU5"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":74,"column":1},"end":{"line":75,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":74,"column":1},"end":{"line":74,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Quantum-Secure Data Transport","position":{"start":{"line":74,"column":1},"end":{"line":74,"column":1}},"key":"sExGJTgB6i"}],"key":"d4d7yq9kDC"},{"type":"text","value":":\nThe DoDIN is transitioning to Quantum Local Area Networks (QLANs) that transmit entangled photons over existing fiber architecture. MEG fibers can power the local quantum repeaters necessary to amplify signals across the DoDIN without introducing electrical noise that could disrupt quantum states.","position":{"start":{"line":74,"column":1},"end":{"line":74,"column":1}},"key":"YDbskytr9F"}],"key":"igrNEj5MWN"}],"key":"TIfeJMywjV"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":76,"column":1},"end":{"line":77,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":76,"column":1},"end":{"line":76,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Neural-Digital Translation","position":{"start":{"line":76,"column":1},"end":{"line":76,"column":1}},"key":"B9fHjPbvhe"}],"key":"vobwPNd7FS"},{"type":"text","value":":\nThrough programs like NESD (Neural Engineering System Design), the DoD implements interfaces that translate “biological electrochemical language” into the “ones and zeros” of the DoDIN. This allows direct, high-bandwidth communication between the brain and military information systems, such as the Combined Joint All-Domain Command and Control (CJADC2).","position":{"start":{"line":76,"column":1},"end":{"line":76,"column":1}},"key":"Dzm0qIU0Ag"}],"key":"qSW0LYcXH4"}],"key":"krY5W2mns8"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":78,"column":1},"end":{"line":80,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":78,"column":1},"end":{"line":78,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Persistent Monitoring and Resilience","position":{"start":{"line":78,"column":1},"end":{"line":78,"column":1}},"key":"eeKVBnRuSy"}],"key":"UgkFYcfEfM"},{"type":"text","value":":\nThe DoDIN uses “network as a sensor” technology where fibers detect tampering or environmental shifts. MEG-powered neural interfaces integrated into this mesh provide real-time situational awareness for operators within the DoDIN’s zero-trust architecture.","position":{"start":{"line":78,"column":1},"end":{"line":78,"column":1}},"key":"GUfRBXdnkx"}],"key":"VqBLxLWRuC"}],"key":"QPhvzfrtjb"}],"key":"QC5hZLvQ1T"},{"type":"thematicBreak","position":{"start":{"line":81,"column":1},"end":{"line":81,"column":1}},"key":"YFRdb2M5xN"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":83,"column":1},"end":{"line":83,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Authorizing moisture-driven fiber neural interfaces on the Department of Defense Information Network (DoDIN) requires navigating a rigorous compliance framework. Because these devices combine medical functions with network connectivity, they are subject to both information technology (IT) and Internet of Medical Things (IoMT) security standards.","position":{"start":{"line":83,"column":1},"end":{"line":83,"column":1}},"key":"Yk3qj9UFIL"}],"key":"eL7NeVzbBU"},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":85,"column":1},"end":{"line":110,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":85,"column":1},"end":{"line":90,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":85,"column":1},"end":{"line":86,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Risk Management Framework (RMF) Authorization:\nThe primary pathway for any device connecting to the DoDIN is the 7-step RMF process, governed by DoDI 8510.01.","position":{"start":{"line":85,"column":1},"end":{"line":85,"column":1}},"key":"QcgEoLpX0v"}],"key":"dNa7flGiph"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":87,"column":1},"end":{"line":90,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":87,"column":1},"end":{"line":87,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Categorization: Systems are categorized based on the impact of a breach to Confidentiality, Integrity, and Availability (CIA).","position":{"start":{"line":87,"column":1},"end":{"line":87,"column":1}},"key":"FKbhdHq2AU"}],"key":"HqmeIqKbD4"}],"key":"jtPo7RPvga"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":88,"column":1},"end":{"line":88,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Control Selection: Neural interfaces must implement specific NIST SP 800-53 security controls tailored for bio-electronic data.","position":{"start":{"line":88,"column":1},"end":{"line":88,"column":1}},"key":"TD2FmH8JoS"}],"key":"oLVqpBu0QF"}],"key":"LhOju93VqF"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":89,"column":1},"end":{"line":90,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ATO (Authorization to Operate): A designated Authorizing Official (AO) must formally accept the residual risk before the device can transmit data on the network.","position":{"start":{"line":89,"column":1},"end":{"line":89,"column":1}},"key":"uUhUmAHuKR"}],"key":"CrOUFIELQk"}],"key":"kwSEii9e0k"}],"key":"gFzgeVKqeA"}],"key":"tjecedUSQY"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":91,"column":1},"end":{"line":96,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":91,"column":1},"end":{"line":92,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"DoDIN Approved Products List (APL):\nTo be eligible for purchase and operation across the DoD, the hardware must typically be listed on the DoDIN APL.","position":{"start":{"line":91,"column":1},"end":{"line":91,"column":1}},"key":"qnZoTpbvJT"}],"key":"l517SuwuJn"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":93,"column":1},"end":{"line":96,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":93,"column":1},"end":{"line":93,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interoperability Certification: Ensures the fiber interface can communicate with existing DoDIN infrastructure without causing network instability.","position":{"start":{"line":93,"column":1},"end":{"line":93,"column":1}},"key":"sA2XfFMCw8"}],"key":"bNT8t37Aep"}],"key":"MP20ESWY4S"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":94,"column":1},"end":{"line":94,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cybersecurity Testing: Conducted at a DISA Testing Center, this involves rigorous vulnerability scanning and penetration testing.","position":{"start":{"line":94,"column":1},"end":{"line":94,"column":1}},"key":"mEumwVNHVt"}],"key":"Vg2XKY25AW"}],"key":"yNqNhm9zYN"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":95,"column":1},"end":{"line":96,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sunset Transition: Note that the DoDIN APL is currently being sunset (phasing out by September 2025) in favor of more dynamic, continuous monitoring processes.","position":{"start":{"line":95,"column":1},"end":{"line":95,"column":1}},"key":"ykkUUam39G"}],"key":"BfrCty6iHb"}],"key":"W3F8OFrqAC"}],"key":"s9RK7tTnm6"}],"key":"TgdazwrgKy"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":97,"column":1},"end":{"line":102,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":97,"column":1},"end":{"line":98,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Medical Device Cybersecurity (MedCOI)\nSince these fibers act as neural interfaces, they must adhere to Defense Health Agency (DHA) protocols for the Medical Community of Interest (MedCOI).","position":{"start":{"line":97,"column":1},"end":{"line":97,"column":1}},"key":"QNriHfZqug"}],"key":"v2T2Q3It8y"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":100,"column":1},"end":{"line":102,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":100,"column":1},"end":{"line":100,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tailored RMF: Standard IT RMF is often adjusted for Medical Device Equipment (MDE) to ensure security measures do not interfere with patient safety or real-time neural modulation.","position":{"start":{"line":100,"column":1},"end":{"line":100,"column":1}},"key":"ZRHBMkh3pf"}],"key":"J3HjRZYGWE"}],"key":"ysnOu3PYC6"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":101,"column":1},"end":{"line":102,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Electronic Medical Device (EMD) Review: If used in secure areas (like a SCIF), devices undergo a 30-day review to assess physical and technical security mitigations.","position":{"start":{"line":101,"column":1},"end":{"line":101,"column":1}},"key":"oBFQaDRYRx"}],"key":"FPCD8BBUsn"}],"key":"mUN0ttm5Y5"}],"key":"giOjV4J7jM"}],"key":"sZ4Jjnz7Na"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":103,"column":1},"end":{"line":107,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":103,"column":1},"end":{"line":103,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Supply Chain & Contractor Compliance (CMMC 2.0):","position":{"start":{"line":103,"column":1},"end":{"line":103,"column":1}},"key":"ceiq2JSgvZ"}],"key":"ym3zb1vQaY"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":104,"column":1},"end":{"line":107,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":104,"column":1},"end":{"line":104,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The entities developing and maintaining these neural interfaces must meet Cybersecurity Maturity Model Certification (CMMC) standards.","position":{"start":{"line":104,"column":1},"end":{"line":104,"column":1}},"key":"ku16KEMqQh"}],"key":"ldvw9Ve3Du"}],"key":"gtw7ghXkzM"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":105,"column":1},"end":{"line":105,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Level 3 Certification: Given that neural data is often considered “breakthrough, unique, or advanced technology,” contractors likely require Level 3 CMMC, involving government-led assessments against NIST SP 800-172.","position":{"start":{"line":105,"column":1},"end":{"line":105,"column":1}},"key":"FCoSict09Y"}],"key":"tcAE63XHls"}],"key":"OIo0ysNGbN"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":106,"column":1},"end":{"line":107,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Phase 1 Rollout: As of November 10, 2025, CMMC requirements are being actively included in all new DoD solicitations.","position":{"start":{"line":106,"column":1},"end":{"line":106,"column":1}},"key":"p9c8TdrAor"}],"key":"uyqrOItEmA"}],"key":"YGJzWAYiRE"}],"key":"LamDmEWH6r"}],"key":"zUnlseHw5u"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":108,"column":1},"end":{"line":110,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":108,"column":1},"end":{"line":108,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Technical Implementation Standards","position":{"start":{"line":108,"column":1},"end":{"line":108,"column":1}},"key":"eZtV6grhr7"}],"key":"XrdjASdITy"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":109,"column":1},"end":{"line":110,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":109,"column":1},"end":{"line":109,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"STIG Compliance: Systems must follow Security Technical Implementation Guides (STIGs) for the underlying operating system and application layers.","position":{"start":{"line":109,"column":1},"end":{"line":109,"column":1}},"key":"ZskJSAVxb1"}],"key":"kytwMpHyOA"}],"key":"TBoXhgcCo3"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":110,"column":1},"end":{"line":110,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"PPSM (Ports, Protocols, and Services Management): All network traffic generated by the neural interface must be cataloged and governed under DoDI 8551.01 to prevent unauthorized data exfiltration.","position":{"start":{"line":110,"column":1},"end":{"line":110,"column":1}},"key":"nVqcBsJmHI"}],"key":"hwHQ0ZAckb"}],"key":"FomLGsJg4D"}],"key":"UEoipXoN7K"}],"key":"BhSybjUDy6"}],"key":"yN6CDKJ04B"}],"key":"IlYUtgfniZ"}],"key":"F0Z8rXoWrt"},"references":{"cite":{"order":[],"data":{}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"prev":{"title":"HyperQUEEN","url":"/hyperqueen","group":"Algorithms"},"next":{"title":"A Pluto.jl notebook","url":"/index2-1","group":"Harvest"}}},"domain":"http://localhost:3000"}